			"notes": "I will no longer be supporting 1.18, so either someone needs to make a PR, or you all wait a couple months when im done the multi-version merge.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `useModelShape` is now enabled by default. This means that all blocks will be creating there culling shape based on there model. This is a bit of an experimental change, however the performance gains are insane. Stuff like flower pots on top of fences will now cull the top of the fence.  \n- `BakedOpacity` now has `setCullingShape` & `canSetCullingShape` \n- Thanks @HhiPyrene for the  updated Simplified translation changes\n\n**Fixes:**\n- Fixed sodium menu missing a toggle for rain/snow culling  \n- [#148](https://github.com/fxmorin/MoreCulling/issues/148) & [#149](https://github.com/fxmorin/MoreCulling/issues/149) - No longer rely on FAPI  \n- [#119](https://github.com/fxmorin/MoreCulling/issues/119) - Move `cloth-config` to `embedded`  \n- [#143](https://github.com/fxmorin/MoreCulling/issues/143) - Fix Rails and Ladders not culling correctly"
		},
